 their independent  impartial view because i can't trust the  moment ministers are guided by one  principle and one principle alone which  is public health before party politics  so this is not good for the country i  think boris johnson ought to go in the  national interest i know we'll be stuck  with a conservative government for a bit  longer and i hope it is just a bit  longer and the responsibility ultimately  falls on us to show the voters that  we're not complacent we're not waiting  for government to fall into our laps we  don't think it's the case that because  the tories are in a mess that people  just flock to labour by default we want  to win people's trust i mean that's why  yesterday kierstama did a big speech  about the future of health and social  care he could have just banged on about  boris johnson for 20 minutes and  everyone would have loved it but he did  that speech to show the country that  labor has a plan labour has a vision for  the country labor is ready for  government indeed well he's made  speeches like that before and it doesn't  seem to be working because um this  morning's opinion poll which puts you  ten  points ahead as a party  has a rather interesting finding and let  me just quote what the director of  research is opinion says when we tested  possible successes to johnson while most  of the cabinet got negative ratings  nearly half of people say they think  rishi sunak would be a good prime  minister a figure that is higher than  both labour's vote share and kierstarm's  approval rating so actually  your vote lead is really more to do with  johnson's unpopularity than the uh the  the the idea that the voters have had a  come to jesus moment labor and  discovered that labour is is the what  they're looking for well we're  absolutely not complete complacent care  is not complacent whenever we get new  polls out showing a labour lead kiara is  the first person to say we're not  looking at this through rose tinted  glasses we've got work to do still to  win back trust but that's why in the new  year he did a big speech outlining his  vision for the country and the  principles that would underpin a labour  government followed up very quickly by  substantial speech about health and  social care you'll be hearing more about  this from kier and from the rest of the  shadow covenant over this year because  this is the year where we will be saying  to the country we've got a terrible  government the country deserves a better  alternative here is labour's alternative  and that's where we'll be in 2022. all  right one quick last question um labour  backbencher barry gardner received over  400 000 pounds from a source linked to  the chinese communist party for his  political work  will he and any other mp who benefited  from that kind of money be required to  return it by the labour party  i don't know that we can require him to  to return it i do think this is very  serious  i do think that we've got a real issue  here uh which extends beyond one labour  mp it's also about access to government  ministers that's why to be honest both  of our parties aren't treating this as a  party political knockabout it's being  taken very seriously by the leadership  of both parties we can't have a  situation where a foreign government  particularly one hostile to  britain's interests on a number of  levels is able to directly interfere in  our politics that's what we've got to  draw a line under and i hope that very  quickly we'll be having a full review of  what's happened the lessons that need to  be learned we also need to act very  quickly  the intelligence security committee made  a whole number of recommendations in  relation to the russia report many of  those haven't yet been implemented so i  think there's an urgency to act national  security's got to come first we're  streeting thank you very much for your  time this morning thank you

